# Site-specific build settings & secrets, layered over the tracked defaults.
#
# Copy to `sdkconfig.local`, which is gitignored, & edit there:
#
#     cp sdkconfig.local.example sdkconfig.local
#
# Nothing in *this* file may be a real credential -- it is committed. ESP-IDF also loads
# `sdkconfig.local.<target>`, so per-chip overrides layer the same way. The full
# precedence order is in the note in CMakeLists.txt.

# --- Where this device fetches its firmware --------------------------------------------
# The host must appear in the server certificate's SAN list, & must match the
# OTA_BASE_URL that tools/publish.sh writes into the manifest.
CONFIG_APP_OTA_BASE_URL="https://nas.lan:8443/fw"

# --- Calendars, optional ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Seeded into NVS on first boot only; the web page edits the list after that. Each entry
# is name,colour,url; the URL is Google's "Secret address in iCal format" & is a secret.
#CONFIG_APP_CAL_SEED="Family,blue,https://calendar.google.com/calendar/ical/.../basic.ics"
CONFIG_APP_CAL_TZ="GMT0IST,M3.5.0/1,M10.5.0"

# --- Development ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stay awake while on USB power, so the board can be reflashed without holding BOOT.
#CONFIG_APP_CYCLE_SLEEP_ON_USB=n

# --- The provisioning AP's passphrase salt ---------------------------------------------
# Mixed with the MAC to derive the setup passphrase. The tracked default is published
# with this repository, & the SSID advertises the MAC -- so a device left on the default
# has a passphrase anyone can compute. Set your own before commissioning a board.
CONFIG_APP_CFG_AP_PASS_SALT=""
